# Copy to /etc/hivepilot/shared.env and fill in the vars that must apply to
# EVERY hivepilot-* service, then source it from the FIRST line of each
# /etc/conf.d/hivepilot-* file (see the `conf.d/hivepilot-*.example` files
# in this directory — each already starts with the sourcing line below):
#
#   [ -f /etc/hivepilot/shared.env ] && . /etc/hivepilot/shared.env
#
# WHY this file exists: OpenRC services each run in their own isolated env
# silo (their own /etc/conf.d/hivepilot-<svc> file only) — there is no
# shared process environment across hivepilot-api/-scheduler/-telegram/
# -slack/-discord. A var set in only SOME of those files is invisible to the
# others. This bit a real deployment: IS_SANDBOX=1 was set in
# hivepilot-api and hivepilot-scheduler but NOT hivepilot-telegram, and
# since a Telegram approval callback RESUMES the pipeline INSIDE the
# telegram process, the developer stage ran without IS_SANDBOX and failed.
# See deploy/openrc/README.md, "Env silos — read this".
#
# Rule of thumb: anything a RESUMED pipeline needs (any approval-callback
# path — Telegram/Slack/Discord) must live here, not in a single service's
# conf.d file, because you cannot predict in advance which service process
# will be the one that resumes a given run.
#
# This file may hold sensitive values -- after copying, run:
#   chmod 600 /etc/hivepilot/shared.env

# export IS_SANDBOX=1
# export HIVEPILOT_CLAUDE_CAPTURE_USAGE=false

# --- Telegram door tokens (HP-130d) ---
# Keep the live single-bot path: leave these unset. hivepilot-telegram
# still holds HIVEPILOT_TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN (legacy noxysdevbot).
#
# Multi-token mode is per-process: telegram_multi_token_mode() is true only
# when THAT process sees 2+ distinct door tokens. Put the four tokens here
# (sourced by every /etc/conf.d/hivepilot-*) so api / scheduler / telegram
# agree. Setting them only in hivepilot-telegram splits routing -- the bot
# drops forum thread ids while scheduler notifications still use topics.
#
# There is NO automatic cutover. Shipping these examples does not enable
# four bots, does not wipe the topic registry, and does not delete leftover
# forum topics 2118-2121. Live cutover needs Jerome's four BotFather
# tokens + CoS GO -- they are not included in this repo. After that:
# restart api+scheduler+telegram together, then
# `hivepilot topics cutover --yes` and prune/delete 2118-2121 by hand.
# export HIVEPILOT_TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN_INBOX=<inbox-bot-token>
# export HIVEPILOT_TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN_APPROVALS=<approvals-bot-token>
# export HIVEPILOT_TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN_RUNS=<runs-bot-token>
# export HIVEPILOT_TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN_ALERTS=<alerts-bot-token>
